{"title":"Minimum Number of Moves to Make Palindrome","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"You are given a string `s` made of lowercase English letters. In one **move** you may choose any two **adjacent** characters and swap them.\n\nReturn the minimum number of moves needed to turn `s` into a palindrome. The input is guaranteed to be convertible into a palindrome by some sequence of adjacent swaps (equivalently, at most one letter occurs an odd number of times).\n\nThis problem appeared as a \"minimum adjacent swaps to make a string a palindrome\" question in an online assessment.","inputFormat":"A single line containing the string `s`.","outputFormat":"Print a single integer: the minimum number of adjacent swaps.","constraints":["1 ≤ |s| ≤ 2000","`s` consists of lowercase English letters","`s` can be rearranged into a palindrome"],"examples":[{"input":"abcab","output":"1","explanation":"Swap the first two characters: `abcab` → `bacab`, which is a palindrome. It is not already a palindrome, so at least one move is needed."},{"input":"aabcb","output":"3","explanation":"`aabcb` → `abacb` → `baacb` → `bacab`. Three swaps reach the palindrome `bacab`, and no sequence of two swaps does."},{"input":"level","output":"0","explanation":"The string is already a palindrome."}],"tests":[{"input":"a","output":"0"},{"input":"aa","output":"0"},{"input":"aba","output":"0"},{"input":"baa","output":"1"},{"input":"aab","output":"1"},{"input":"abab","output":"1"},{"input":"aabb","output":"2"},{"input":"abcba","output":"0"},{"input":"zzzzzzzz","output":"0"},{"input":"cc","output":"0"},{"input":"acc","output":"1"},{"input":"aaa","output":"0"},{"input":"bbbb","output":"0"},{"input":"aaaa","output":"0"},{"input":"acccc","output":"2"},{"input":"ababa","output":"0"},{"input":"abbab","output":"1"},{"input":"bbbbbb","output":"0"},{"input":"","output":"500000"},{"input":"","output":"960562"},{"input":"","output":"13801"},{"input":"","output":"87395"}],"complexity":{"time":"O(n^2)","space":"O(n)"},"hints":["Look at the last character. It must be mirrored by an equal character at the front half. Which occurrence is cheapest to bring to the front?","Greedily take the first occurrence of the last character: moving it to index 0 costs exactly its index in swaps. Then delete both ends and repeat on the shorter string.","If the last character occurs only once in what remains, it is the middle character of the final palindrome. Moving it to the center costs `len // 2` swaps; remove it and continue."],"starters":{"python":"import sys\n\n\ndef min_moves_to_palindrome(s: str) -> int:\n    # Write your solution here\n    return 0\n\n\ndef main():\n    s = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    print(min_moves_to_palindrome(s))\n\n\nmain()\n","javascript":"function minMovesToPalindrome(s) {\n  // Write your solution here\n  return 0\n}\n\nconst s = input.trim()\nconsole.log(String(minMovesToPalindrome(s)))\n","cpp":"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint minMovesToPalindrome(string s) {\n    // Write your solution here\n    return 0;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n    cout << minMovesToPalindrome(s) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static int minMovesToPalindrome(String s) {\n        // Write your solution here\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String s = br.readLine().trim();\n        System.out.println(minMovesToPalindrome(s));\n    }\n}\n"},"reconstructed":false}